  "title": "F major needs one flat",
  "summary": "Build a major scale on F and the one black key is a flat, B♭.",
  "minutes": 5,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Building F major",
      "body": "Start on F and follow W W H W W W H: F, G, A, then a half step to the black key. Each letter is used once, and A is already taken, so this note is **B♭**, not A♯. Then C, D, E and F. So F major is **F G A B♭ C D E F**.\n\n**Why it matters:** this is why songs in F use B♭, and why band charts in F say B♭, never A♯.",
